{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310744,"nonce":"/o3ZCykU1vflYJDaaC88TQbt08Q=","title":"Two latent rayzor runtime/codegen bugs surfaced while writing the streaming-decode fix (97398cc), worked around there but NOT root-fixed. ...","message":"Both found 2026-06-15 implementing `BPETokenizer.decodeStreamStep`\n(commit 97398cc). Worked around in nue; the underlying compiler/runtime\ndefects remain.\n\n**BUG 1 — wasm anon-struct return drops a String field.**\n`function f():{delta:String, carry:Bytes} { ... return {delta:d, carry:c}; }`\nthen at the call site `var r = f(); r.delta` reads **empty** on wasm\n(r.carry / non-String fields appeared fine). The producing function\ncomputed `delta` correctly (verified by tracing inside f), so the loss is\nin the anon-struct construction/field-access codegen on the String field,\nnot the value. Symptom in the wild: streamed output was entirely blank\nwhile the per-token decode trace showed correct text. WORKAROUND: return\nthe String directly and pass the other value via a single-element holder\n`Array` (mutate `holder[0]`); arrays capture/mutate by reference on wasm\n(the same pattern GenerationLoop already used for its int counters). Likely\nsame family as [[bugs_wasm_generic_string_concat]] (generic/struct String\noperand drops). Native was NOT shown to have this (the wasm-only blank).\n\n**BUG 2 — rayzor.Bytes.blit has OPPOSITE direction native vs wasm.**\n`rayzor.Bytes.blit(srcPos, dest, destPos, len)` (haxe-std/rayzor/Bytes.hx:132).\nThe call `combined.blit(cn, pieceBytes, 0, pbLen)` intended to copy\npieceBytes -\u003e combined[cn..]. On **wasm** it did exactly that (standard\nHaxe semantics: `this`=dest). On **native** it produced garbage (combined\nleft at its alloc-init, deltas came out as runs of 0x20 spaces of the\ncorrect length) — consistent with native copying in the reverse direction\n(`this`=source, per the extern's param NAMES) or otherwise not writing\n`combined`. So the two runtime impls of blit disagree on direction. The\nextern signature param names (srcPos / dest / destPos) and its doc comment\n(\"Copies bytes from source to this buffer\") are mutually contradictory,\nwhich is the smell. WORKAROUND: avoid blit entirely — explicit\n`for (i in 0...n) dst.set(p+i, src.get(i))` loops (buffers were tiny).\nNEEDS root-fix: make native + wasm blit agree (pick standard Haxe\n`this`=dest) and fix the extern's param names/doc. Audit other blit call\nsites for native/wasm divergence.\n\n**Debugging method that found both (reusable):** a `Sys.getEnv`-gated\n`Sys.println(\"[dss] ... deltaLen=\" + delta.length + \" delta=[\" + delta + \"]\")`\ninside the producing function pinned (1) instantly (delta correct inside f,\nempty at the call site =\u003e return path) and (2) (delta = N spaces =\u003e the\nbuffer feeding it was never written =\u003e blit). Trace INSIDE the producer and\ncompare to the consumer.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_wasm_anon_struct_and_blit` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}